        {
          "published_at": "2026-11-07T06:15:51.595Z",
          "url": "https://x.com/thorstenball/status/2118950540021203169",
          "topic": "Running full-stack coding agents on remote headless environments",
          "text": "This is blowing my mind.\n\nIs this true, you can't run Postgres or MySQL in Claude Code and Cursor?\n\nYou can run your full stack in orbs. We run multiple dev servers/services, Postgres, Redis, Docker in there.\n\nAnd hard disagree on 2nd point: the \"problems of remote coding\" *are* solved.\n\nFor one, you're no longer coding :) No need anymore to get LSPs or other editor-centric tooling running. Or an editor! That was always a huge pain in the ass, now the whole ass is gone.\n\nAnd everything else that was painful about setting up remote envs is truly no longer painful with agents. Configuring services to work in there, making headless browsers work, making headless anything work -- super easy now.\n\nIt sounds like Armin & Ben haven't tried it, but I urge you: put your code on a remote box, headless, ask an agent to run through it end to end. It will blow your mind.\n\nEverything has changed.",
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "photo",
              "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWgEEfOW0AAfEvZ?format=webp&name=large",
              "width": 542,
